From 66ab0cf356e4c9491c6fa266d6990c90ed2cdd43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SG Quality Lead R8 <danswett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:23:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] CI S2: split the Playwright system-packages action so FULL
 can never write a cache (CodeQL on #4254)

CodeQL did not see through the save input that gated the cache save inside playwright-system-packages, which full.yml (privileged) calls. So the action is now
RESTORE-ONLY: no save input, no cache/save step; it outputs the archives cache's exact key (cache-key) and whether the archives are ready (cache-ready). The save
is a new action, playwright-system-packages-save, that holds only the cache/save step and is called ONLY by ci.yml: once after each restore call (pwa-ui, pwa-e2e),
if: always() && steps.system-packages.outputs.cache-ready == 'true', exactly the timing of the old in-action save. full.yml calls only the restore action.

Tests (red-first): full.yml has no cache save, never references the save action, calls only the restore action; the restore action has no cache/save and no save
input; the save action holds only the save; ci.yml has one save step per restore call, each gated on always() and the ready output (proved red by calling the save
action from full.yml, by putting a save back in the restore action, and by dropping a ci.yml save). test.sh's checks follow the split and hold in every state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
